  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA cold front will move east across the area late today and into\ntonight, delivering low-end rain chances to portions of\nNortheast Ohio and Northwest Pennsylvania. Any rain\namounts will be light. Otherwise, dry weather is generally\nfavored across the area for the next several days thanks to \nmid-level dry air with the frontal passage and high pressure\nbuilding over the region through the middle of the week.\n\nTemperatures will fluctuate a bit this week, although highs will\nlargely be in the 60s and lower 70s. Monday will be the coolest\nday of the week with highs in the low to mid 60s expected. \nOvernight lows will be quite cold Monday night due to efficient \nradiational cooling with forecast temps falling into the upper \n30s and lower 40s. Locally colder temperatures as chilly as the \nmid 30s are possible in typical cold spots Monday night \nincluding portions of interior NW PA and the Central Highlands, \nwhere there could be patchy to areas of frost. This will be the \nfirst opportunity for frost headlines, although there is still \nuncertainty with how widespread any frost will be. Otherwise, \novernight lows will be in the 40s each night.",
